  "name": "Earth Release: Sandwich Technique",
  "type": "jutsu",
  "img": "icons/svg/book.svg",
  "system": {
    "identifier": "earth-release-sandwich-technique",
    "description": "<p>You conjure two large constructs of earth of your design on either side of a chosen point you can see in range and slam them into one another crushing everything in between. All creatures in a 20-foot Cube centered on the chosen point must make a Strength saving throw to resist being crushed.</p>\n<p>On a failed save, affected creatures take 2d12 earth damage and are Dazed on a failed Save or half as much damage on a success. If more than one creature is affected by this jutsu, on a failed save, all affected creatures become Bruised.</p>\n<p>At Higher Ranks: For each rank you cast this jutsu above D-Rank, increase the cost of this jutsu by 3 and the damage by 1d6. If this jutsu is cast at B-Rank, you can select a second point you can see in range. A creature can only be affected by this jutsu once per casting. If this jutsu is cast at S-Rank, a creature that fails their saving throw by 5 or more is Stunned until the end of their next turn, instead of Dazed.</p>",
